ity is actually  shared  by the integrated service as well as  you know the underlying data store which  is s30  and this is unique um in the sense that  we don't have an intermediate  filtering fleet there's advantages and  disadvantages of this and we can talk  about it  but one of the advantages of this is of  course cost customers aren't really  spending a tremendous amount more money  over the  normal processing of your data and this  is what they like  here's some screens i'm running out of  time so i'm going to quickly go over  these screens but here's some screens on  how you can actually use lake formation  to specify  the permissions these permissions look  like standard grant and remote  permissions that you see in a database  you can do it at the column level and  then depending on  you know the analyst and what they're  able to see what these screens are  actually showing you is that  you know one analyst is able to see you  know a fraction of the columns in this  case they're  uh if you look on the screen shot on the  left hand side there's seven columns  that this analyst can see and  um you know there's another uh analyst  um that's gonna access it through a  different engine might see fewer columns  and then the data scientists can access  it through notebooks and and see all the  columns for example  except for pii yeah  you can also through our console  monitor all the use of that data lake  who's accessing what with all the  metadata so you have a centralized  affiliate place for  all your audit logs um so if you have a  compliance officer coming in and saying  hey who  accessed what in the past um you know in  the past  month or in the past year you can  actually give them a compliance audit  rather than trying to you know create  this manual yourself  and the other cool thing about this and  this is the piece that i think i want to  you know kind of spend a little time on  is once you get into the data lake world  it's no longer about you know 